  {
   "title": "Single transaction for the whole transfer",
   "context": "The legacy opens one SqlTransaction after the same-account check and rolls it back at four rejection points before any write; it commits after the insert in TRANSFERENCIAS.",
   "decision": "RealizarTransferencia runs in one transactional boundary generated from unit_of_work (begin at line 34, commit at line 102, rollbacks at lines 43, 52, 62 and 70). The same-account check (RULE-005) runs before opening it, as in the legacy, so it touches no database. No savepoints, so no UnitOfWork port is needed.",
   "consequences": "Debit, credit and registration are atomic. Every rejection leaves the tables unchanged, as the recorded traces show."
  },
  {
   "title": "Commission calculation is pure domain logic",
   "context": "ComisionService.Calcular is a static, stateless function (uplift assessment: uplift).",
   "decision": "Port it as a domain service inside the use case using BigDecimal: flat 0.50 when monto <= 1000.00, otherwise monto * 0.001 rounded to 2 decimals with RoundingMode.HALF_UP (away from zero for positives, as MidpointRounding.AwayFromZero), cap at 5.00, then +1.00 when tipo equals \"INM\" (case-sensitive), so INM can reach 6.00.",
   "consequences": "Not a port and no external call. Behaviour is covered by the traces (500 PRO -> 0.50, 1005 PRO -> 1.01, 9000 PRO -> 5.00, 7000 INM -> 6.00)."
  },
  {
   "title": "Data moves to the target database",
   "context": "The WebForms pages are rewritten and the legacy has no stored procedures; it uses inline SQL on CUENTAS and TRANSFERENCIAS.",
   "decision": "data_strategy is migration: both tables are recreated in the target database with snake_case names and the legacy precision (DECIMAL(13,2) balance, DECIMAL(11,2) amount, DECIMAL(7,2) commission, VARCHAR(10) accounts, CHAR(3) type).",
   "consequences": "A one-off data migration is needed. Replay of the golden master compares the tables before and after each recorded case."
  },
  {
   "title": "Sequential transfer number kept as MAX+1 inside the transaction",
   "context": "The legacy computes TRF_NUMERO as ISNULL(MAX(TRF_NUMERO),0)+1 within the transaction, with no sequence or lock.",
   "decision": "Preserve the rule (numbers start at 1 and follow the current maximum) in nextNumero, executed in the same transaction as the insert.",
   "consequences": "Concurrent transfers can compute the same number, as in the legacy. The primary key makes the second insert fail instead of duplicating. A sequence or stricter locking is a future decision, not part of this migration."
  },
  {
   "title": "Redirect to the receipt becomes a response with the number",
   "context": "After commit the legacy sets lblComision and lblMensaje and then redirects to Comprobante.aspx?numero=N, so those labels never reach the user.",
   "decision": "The POST returns numero, comision and mensaje 'TRANSFERENCIA REALIZADA'. The client then calls GET /transferencias/{numero}/comprobante. Rejections return the legacy message with the stable error code.",
